{"version":"0.1","documentType":"opinion","source":{"kind":"lrb_html","caseId":"2011_05364","path":"opinions/coa/2011/2011_05364.htm","publicationStatus":"published"},"header":{"title":"People v DiGuglielmo","slipOpinion":"2011 NY Slip Op 05364 [17 NY3d 771]","officialCitation":null,"court":"Court of Appeals","decisionDate":null},"appearances":[],"opinions":[{"kind":"majority","author":null,"label":null,"joiners":[],"blocks":[{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"{**17 NY3d at 772}"},{"type":"text","text":" OPINION OF THE COURT"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Memorandum. "},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"The order of the Appellate Division should be affirmed. "},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Assuming that defendant made a specific request for the material alleged to be exculpatory, we find no reasonable possibility that any failure to disclose it contributed to the "},{"type":"text","text":"verdict ("},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","text":"see People v Vilardi"}]},{"type":"text","text":", 76 NY2d 67, 77 [1990]). Moreover, we reject defendant's claim that the evidence supporting his conviction of depraved indifference murder is legally insufficient because of our decision in "},{"type":"link","href":"../2006/2006_05233.htm","children":[{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","text":"People v Feingold"}]},{"type":"text","text":" (7 NY3d 288"}]},{"type":"text","text":" [2006]). The standard enunciated in "},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","text":"Feingold"}]},{"type":"text","text":" simply does not apply retroactively to cases on collateral review ("},{"type":"link","href":"../2006/2006_08284.htm","children":[{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","text":"see Policano v Herbert"}]},{"type":"text","text":", 7"},{"type":"text","text":"{**17 NY3d at 773}"},{"type":"text","text":" NY3d 588"}]},{"type":"text","text":", 603-604 [2006]), and defendant's claim that such a result violates the Federal Due Process Clause is without merit ("},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","text":"Wainwright v Stone"}]},{"type":"text","text":", 414 US 21, 23-24 [1973]). "},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Chief Judge Lippman and Judges Ciparick, Graffeo, Read, Smith, Pigott and Jones concur. "},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Order affirmed in a memorandum. "},{"type":"text","text":" "}],"provenance":{"startLine":7,"endLine":17}}]}],"footnotes":[],"disposition":null,"renderingHints":{"hasOfficialPageMarkers":true,"hasAppearances":false,"hasFootnotes":false,"hasSeparateOpinions":false},"debug":{"diagnostics":[]}}
